### GET /v1/matchmaking/tickets/{ticketId} — fetch ticket status
###
### When to use: to poll the current state of a matchmaking ticket (status,
### skill, searchRange). Requires a Bearer token; the ticket must belong to the
### authenticated player.
###
### How to use: run POST /v1/matchmaking/tickets first (captures `ticketId`),
### then run the request below.
###
### Expected: 200 with the ticket JSON.
### Error cases: unknown id → 404; ticket owned by another player → 403.

@apiBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Happy path — expect 200
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error case — unknown id → expect 404
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/does-not-exist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error case — ticket of another player → expect 403
### (log in as a different playerId in auth-service and use that token,
### querying a ticketId created by player-1)
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
